# Descriptions précises des planches d'espèces (anglais, pour le générateur d'images).
# Chaque texte dit QUOI dessiner, COMMENT, et ce qu'il NE FAUT PAS dessiner (erreurs fréquentes des IA).
# Injecté dans docs/atelier-images.html (ESP_DESC) par tools/esp_inject.py.
D = {
# ---------------- PLANTES TOXIQUES ----------------
"oenanthe": "Hemlock water dropwort (Oenanthe crocata). Left: the upper part of a stout, hollow, grooved green stem (no purple spots) bearing one large leaf that is 3-times pinnate with BROAD, wedge-shaped, toothed leaflets like celery or flat-leaf parsley (NOT finely cut, NOT feathery, NOT carrot-like). Top: one flat compound umbel of small white flowers with 15 to 40 rays. Bottom right: the base of the plant pulled out of mud showing a cluster of 4 to 6 pale cream, swollen, spindle-shaped root tubers hanging from the stem base like fingers; one tuber cut across shows white flesh with a drop of yellow-orange sap.",
"if": "Common yew (Taxus baccata). One twig of yew, nothing else: flat, soft, dark green needles 2 to 3 cm long with a pointed tip, arranged spirally but spreading in two flat rows on each side of the twig, paler green underneath. Several seeds on the twig: each is a fleshy, bright red, cup-shaped aril open at the top, with one dark olive-brown seed visible inside the cup. Inset: one aril enlarged, seen from the side and slightly from above. NO broad leaves anywhere, NO olive or willow leaves, NO cones, NO berries in bunches.",
"digitale": "Foxglove (Digitalis purpurea). Left: a basal rosette of large, oval to lance-shaped, softly hairy grey-green leaves with a wrinkled surface and a network of sunken veins, edges finely toothed. Rising from it: one tall unbranched flower spike with many drooping, tubular, pinkish-purple bell flowers all hanging on ONE side of the stem, buds at the top. Inset: one flower seen from the front showing the paler lower lip with dark purple spots ringed in white inside.",
"douceamere": "Bittersweet nightshade (Solanum dulcamara). A woody-based climbing stem that twines and scrambles (NO tendrils, NO curls). Leaves alternate, dark green, oval-pointed, some with one or two small ear-like lobes at the base. Loose drooping clusters of flowers: 5 swept-back purple petals around a pointed bright yellow cone of stamens. Separate drooping cluster of shiny OVAL berries in mixed stages: green, orange and bright red. Inset: one flower enlarged.",
"muguet": "Lily of the valley (Convallaria majalis). One plant: two broad elliptical leaves with parallel veins, their bases wrapped around each other and around the flower stalk inside a sheath at ground level. A leafless arching flower stalk carrying 6 to 10 small, white, rounded bell-shaped flowers with 6 tiny turned-out tips, all hanging on ONE side. Inset: a later stalk with round, shiny red berries.",
"colchique": "Meadow saffron (Colchicum autumnale), two seasons side by side. Left (autumn): 3 pale lilac-pink, goblet-shaped crocus-like flowers with 6 tepals rising straight from the grass on long white tubes, WITHOUT any leaves. Right (spring): a tight tuft of 3 to 5 broad, glossy, tongue-shaped, strap-like leaves with parallel veins all coming from one point at ground level, with a green egg-shaped seed capsule in the center. Small inset: the corm, a brown-skinned bulb-like tuber.",
"arum": "Lords-and-ladies (Arum maculatum). Left: 3 glossy arrow-shaped leaves on long stalks, net-veined, some with scattered dark purple-black spots. Center: the flower, a pale yellow-green hood (spathe) wrapped around an upright purple-brown finger-like spadix. Right: the summer stage, a short stalk with a dense club-shaped cluster of shiny berries, orange-red, the leaves gone.",
"belladone": "Deadly nightshade (Atropa belladonna). A leafy branch with large oval, pointed, smooth leaves in unequal pairs. Single drooping bell-shaped flowers, brownish-violet outside, greenish inside. Shiny round black berries the size of a cherry, each sitting on a green star-shaped calyx with 5 pointed lobes. Inset: one berry on its 5-pointed green star.",
"cigue": "Poison hemlock (Conium maculatum). Tall smooth hairless hollow stem, bluish-green with many irregular dark purple-red blotches and streaks, covered in a whitish bloom. Large triangular leaves very finely divided, 3 to 4 times pinnate, fern-like. Several small umbels of tiny white flowers. Inset: a section of the stem enlarged showing the purple spots clearly.",
"berce": "Giant hogweed (Heracleum mantegazzianum). A huge plant 3 m tall compared with a small standard hiking boot drawn at its base for scale. Thick hollow stem with dark purple blotches and coarse white bristles. Enormous, deeply cut, jagged leaves up to 1.5 m. One giant flat-topped umbel of white flowers about 50 cm wide like an umbrella. Inset: the purple-spotted bristly stem enlarged.",
"aconit": "Monkshood (Aconitum napellus). Upright stem with dark green leaves deeply divided into 5 to 7 narrow pointed fingers, each finger cut again. Tall dense spike of deep blue-violet flowers, each flower with a large hood-shaped upper sepal like a monk's helmet. Inset: one flower in side view showing the helmet.",
"houx": "Holly (Ilex aquifolium). A branch of thick, very glossy, dark green leathery leaves with wavy edges ending in sharp spines (some upper leaves smooth-edged). Clusters of round, shiny, bright red berries along the twig close to the leaves.",
"fusain": "Spindle (Euonymus europaeus). A twig with green young stems that are square in section with 4 thin corky ridges. Opposite oval, finely toothed leaves turning reddish. Hanging fruits: bright pink capsules with 4 rounded lobes, some split open to show seeds wrapped in bright orange flesh. Inset: one open capsule with its orange seed.",
"bryone": "White bryony (Bryonia dioica). A climbing vine with long coiled spring-like tendrils gripping a twig. Rough, hairy, palm-shaped leaves with 5 pointed lobes. Small clusters of pale greenish-white flowers with 5 petals and dark green veins. Bunches of small, round, glossy red berries. Inset: the thick pale swollen root.",
"laurier": "Cherry laurel (Prunus laurocerasus). A branch of large, thick, very glossy, leathery, dark green oblong leaves with a short point and a faintly toothed edge. An upright spike of shiny round berries, some dark red and most glossy black, like small cherries. Inset: an upright spike of small white flowers.",
"laurierrose": "Oleander (Nerium oleander). A leafy shoot with narrow, stiff, leathery, lance-shaped dark green leaves with a pale central vein, in whorls of THREE around the stem. A cluster of pink five-petalled flowers at the tip, petals slightly twisted like a pinwheel. Inset: a long thin bean-like seed pod.",
"datura": "Thorn apple (Datura stramonium). A coarse branching plant with large, irregularly toothed, jagged leaves. One large white trumpet-shaped flower, long tube opening to a pleated 5-pointed rim. Upright green egg-shaped seed capsule the size of a walnut covered in sharp spines, one split open into 4 parts showing small black seeds.",
"ricin": "Castor bean (Ricinus communis). Large palm-shaped leaves with 5 to 11 pointed toothed lobes, reddish-bronze, on long red stalks. A cluster of round spiny reddish seed capsules. Inset: 3 shiny oval seeds marbled in brown and cream like small beetles.",
"veratre": "White false hellebore (Veratrum album). A tall unbranched stem with large broad oval leaves strongly pleated lengthwise like an accordion, ALTERNATE, one by one in a spiral up the stem (NOT in pairs, NOT from the base like wild garlic). At the top: a branched plume of many small star-shaped greenish-white flowers.",
"iris": "Yellow flag iris (Iris pseudacorus). A fan of tall, flat, stiff, sword-shaped grey-green leaves sheathing each other at the base. Tall stems with large bright yellow iris flowers, three broad drooping falls with fine brown veins. Inset: the thick horizontal rhizome with roots in mud.",
# ---------------- PLANTES COMESTIBLES ----------------
"chataignier": "Sweet chestnut (Castanea sativa). A twig with 2 long, narrow, glossy leaves (15 to 25 cm) with a regular row of sharp pointed teeth along the edges and straight parallel side veins. One spiny husk split open in 4: the husk is covered in long, fine, dense needle-like spines like a hedgehog, revealing 2 or 3 shiny brown nuts, flattened on one side, each with a small pale hairy tip. Do NOT draw horse chestnut (no thick husk with few short spikes, no glossy round conker).",
"hetre": "Beech (Fagus sylvatica). A twig with oval leaves with a wavy, untoothed edge fringed with fine hairs and straight parallel veins. Woody spiky husks (cupules) opened into 4 valves, each holding 2 small shiny brown three-sided triangular nuts. Background element on the left: a short section of smooth, pale grey trunk.",
"noisetier": "Hazel (Corylus avellana). A twig with round, double-toothed, softly hairy leaves with a short point. A cluster of 2 or 3 hazelnuts, each wrapped in a green leafy husk with a ragged frilly edge, one nut free and ripe brown. Inset: hanging yellow catkins.",
"eglantier": "Dog rose (Rosa canina). An arching stem with strong HOOKED thorns. Leaves made of 5 to 7 oval toothed leaflets. Smooth, oval, glossy orange-red rose hips 1.5 to 2 cm long, each topped with dried remains of the sepals. Inset: one hip cut lengthwise showing hairy seeds inside, and a pale pink 5-petalled flower.",
"prunellier": "Blackthorn (Prunus spinosa). A dark, very thorny twig with long rigid spines. Small oval toothed leaves. Round blue-black sloes about 1 cm across, covered with a pale dusty waxy bloom. Inset: the small white 5-petalled flowers on a bare thorny twig.",
"aubepine": "Hawthorn (Crataegus monogyna). A thorny twig with leaves deeply cut into 3 to 7 lobes. Clusters of small, oval, dark red haws about 1 cm, each with a tiny dark crown at the tip. Inset: one haw cut open showing a SINGLE hard stone.",
"sorbier": "Rowan (Sorbus aucuparia). A twig with compound leaves of 11 to 15 narrow, toothed leaflets in pairs with one at the tip. Large flat bunches of many small round orange-red berries about 1 cm.",
"gland": "Oak (Quercus robur). A twig with leaves with rounded, irregular lobes and two small ear lobes at the very base of the blade. Two acorns on a long stalk: smooth brown oval nuts sitting in scaly cups. Inset: one acorn out of its cup.",
"ortie": "Stinging nettle (Urtica dioica). An upright SQUARE stem covered with fine stinging hairs. Leaves OPPOSITE in pairs, each pair at right angles to the next, heart-shaped and elongated with a pointed tip and coarse saw-like teeth, also hairy. Drooping strings of tiny greenish flowers from the leaf joints. Inset: the stinging hairs enlarged.",
"pissenlit": "Dandelion (Taraxacum officinale). A flat rosette of long leaves deeply cut into backward-pointing jagged teeth, hairless. Several smooth, hollow, leafless flower stalks, each with ONE yellow flower head of many thin ray florets. One stalk with a round white seed clock. Inset: a broken stalk oozing white milky latex.",
"aildesours": "Wild garlic (Allium ursinum). Several broad, soft, elliptical, bright green leaves, EACH on its own thin separate stalk coming straight from the ground (not on a stem, not in pairs on a stem), shiny on top, dull underneath. One leafless stalk with a round cluster of white six-pointed star-shaped flowers. Inset: the small slender white bulb.",
"mure": "Blackberry bramble (Rubus fruticosus). A long arching prickly cane. Leaves of 3 or 5 toothed leaflets. A cluster of berries at different stages: green, red and ripe glossy black, each berry made of many small round drupelets. Inset: a white-pink 5-petalled flower.",
"framboise": "Wild raspberry (Rubus idaeus). An upright cane with fine, soft bristles. Leaves of 3 to 5 toothed leaflets, white-felted underneath (show one leaf turned over). Red raspberries; one berry pulled off its pale cone-shaped core, showing it is hollow.",
"myrtille": "Bilberry (Vaccinium myrtillus). A small shrub with angular, green, ribbed stems. Small, light green, oval, finely toothed leaves. Round blue-black berries with a dusty bloom and a small flat crown-shaped ring at the tip. Inset: one berry cut open showing purple-red flesh.",
"fraise": "Wild strawberry (Fragaria vesca). A small plant with leaves of 3 toothed oval leaflets on long hairy stalks. A white 5-petalled flower with a yellow center. Small, cone-shaped bright red strawberries with tiny seeds on the surface, the green sepals turned back.",
"sureau": "Elder (Sambucus nigra). Left: a branch with leaves of 5 to 7 oval toothed leaflets and a large flat-topped cluster of tiny creamy white flowers. Right: a hanging cluster of small, round, shiny purple-black berries on red-purple stalks. Inset: a cut twig showing the soft white pith inside and grey corky bark.",
"oseille": "Common sorrel (Rumex acetosa). A small rosette of bright green, smooth, fleshy leaves on long stalks; every leaf blade is ARROWHEAD-shaped: elongated with a blunt tip, and at its base two narrow pointed lobes that point straight DOWN on each side of the stalk (like the barbs of an arrow). Higher up a slender reddish upright stem with a few small arrow-shaped leaves clasping it, topped by loose branched spikes of tiny rusty-red flowers. Inset: one leaf enlarged, flat, showing the two downward-pointing basal lobes clearly. NOT lance-shaped dock leaves, NOT rounded leaf bases, NOT spotted leaves.",
"plantain": "Ribwort plantain (Plantago lanceolata). A rosette of long narrow lance-shaped leaves with 3 to 5 very marked parallel ribs. Several long bare grooved stalks each topped by a short dense brown oval flower spike with a ring of tiny white stamens.",
"cresson": "Watercress (Nasturtium officinale). Hollow, creeping stems floating in a shallow clear stream, roots at the joints. Compound leaves with 3 to 9 rounded, glossy, dark green leaflets, the end leaflet largest. Small clusters of tiny white flowers with 4 petals.",
"tilleul": "Small-leaved lime (Tilia cordata). A twig with heart-shaped, slightly asymmetric, finely toothed leaves with a pointed tip. Hanging clusters of small fragrant creamy-yellow flowers, the flower stalk joined for half its length to a long, pale green, tongue-shaped papery bract.",
"pin": "Scots pine (Pinus sylvestris). A twig with blue-green needles grouped in PAIRS, each pair joined at the base in a small papery sheath (show one pair enlarged). Small brown egg-shaped cones 3 to 6 cm. Background left: a section of upper trunk with orange, flaking, papery bark.",
"bardane": "Greater burdock (Arctium lappa). Huge heart-shaped leaves with a wavy edge, the underside whitish and woolly (show one leaf turned over). A branching stem with round purple thistle-like flower heads and round burs covered in hooked spines. Inset: the long brown taproot.",
"pomme": "Wild crab apple (Malus sylvestris). A twig, sometimes with a short spine, with oval toothed leaves. Small round crab apples 2 to 4 cm, yellow-green with a red blush, on long stalks. Inset: one apple cut across showing the star of seeds.",
"merisier": "Wild cherry (Prunus avium). A twig with oval, toothed, drooping leaves with two small red glands at the top of the leaf stalk. Bunches of shiny red to dark red cherries hanging on long stalks. Background left: a piece of smooth reddish-brown bark peeling in horizontal ribbons.",
"chenopode": "Fat hen (Chenopodium album). An upright plant with diamond-shaped, irregularly toothed leaves, dull grey-green, the young top leaves and the undersides covered with a white mealy powder. Dense spikes of tiny green flower balls.",
"mauve": "Common mallow (Malva sylvestris). Round leaves with 5 to 7 shallow toothed lobes on long stalks. Large pink-purple flowers with 5 notched petals, each petal striped with dark purple veins. Inset: the flat round seed head like a small wheel of cheese.",
"lierreterrestre": "Ground ivy (Glechoma hederacea). A creeping square stem rooting at the joints, with small round kidney-shaped leaves with rounded teeth, in opposite pairs. Small violet-blue tubular two-lipped flowers in groups at the leaf joints.",
"arbousier": "Strawberry tree (Arbutus unedo). A twig with glossy, leathery, finely toothed dark green leaves and red twigs. Round fruits 2 cm covered in small bumps, at all stages: yellow, orange, bright red. A hanging cluster of small white bell-shaped flowers.",
"figuebarbarie": "Prickly pear (Opuntia ficus-indica). Two flat oval fleshy green pads joined together, dotted with areoles bearing tiny tufts of hair-like bristles. Oval fruits growing on the rim of the top pad, green to orange-red, covered with tiny bristle tufts. Inset: one fruit enlarged showing the bristle tufts.",
"pinparasol": "Stone pine (Pinus pinea). Left: the small silhouette of the whole tree with its flat umbrella-shaped crown. Right: a twig with long paired needles and a large heavy rounded brown cone 10 to 15 cm, its scales slightly open. Inset: 3 hard-shelled pine nuts and one shelled kernel.",
"thym": "Common thyme (Thymus vulgaris). A small woody sub-shrub 20 cm high with many thin stems. Tiny narrow grey-green leaves with edges rolled under, in pairs. Small clusters of tiny pale pink-lilac flowers at the tips.",
"romarin": "Rosemary (Salvia rosmarinus). A woody twig densely covered with narrow needle-like leaves, dark green on top, white underneath, edges rolled under. Small pale blue two-lipped flowers along the twig.",
"asperge": "Wild asparagus (Asparagus acutifolius). Left: a tangle of thin stems with clusters of short, stiff, prickly needle-like green cladodes. Right: 3 thin wild asparagus spears emerging from the ground at the base of the plant, green to purple, with a tight scaly tip.",
"airelle": "Lingonberry (Vaccinium vitis-idaea). A low evergreen shrub with small, oval, leathery, glossy dark green leaves with rolled edges; one leaf turned over shows tiny dark dots underneath. Clusters of round glossy bright red berries at the tips.",
"epilobe": "Fireweed (Chamaenerion angustifolium). A tall upright stem with narrow lance-shaped leaves arranged in a spiral, the side veins joining in loops along the edge. A long tapering spike of bright pink-magenta 4-petalled flowers, buds at the top. Inset: a seed pod splitting to release silky white plumes.",
"salicorne": "Glasswort (Salicornia europaea). A small fleshy plant without visible leaves, made of bright green jointed cylindrical segments like small branched candelabras, growing upright from grey tidal mud. Inset: a few segments enlarged.",
"argousier": "Sea buckthorn (Hippophae rhamnoides). A very thorny twig with narrow silvery-grey willow-like leaves. Bright orange oval berries packed tightly all along the twig, almost hiding it.",
"massette": "Bulrush, cattail (Typha latifolia). A clump growing in shallow water: tall flat ribbon-like leaves sheathing each other at the base. Long stems topped by a thick dark brown cylindrical sausage-shaped seed head, with a thin spike above it. Inset: the white starchy rhizome and a young shoot.",
# ---------------- CHAMPIGNONS ----------------
"phalloide": "Death cap (Amanita phalloides). One whole mushroom dug out with its base: smooth olive-green to yellowish cap with faint radial streaks; free, crowded WHITE gills; white stem with a thin drooping skirt-like ring and faint olive zigzag pattern; at the base a large white membranous sac-like volva wrapping a bulb. Second specimen cut lengthwise showing white flesh and the volva. Third: a young egg-shaped specimen still inside its white volva.",
"tuemouches": "Fly agaric (Amanita muscaria). One whole mushroom: bright red cap scattered with white wart-like flakes; white gills; white stem with a hanging white ring; swollen bulbous base ringed with rows of white warts. Second specimen cut lengthwise showing white flesh with a yellow-orange layer under the red skin.",
"galere": "Funeral bell (Galerina marginata). A clump of small mushrooms growing on a mossy rotting stump: smooth, honey-brown to tawny caps 2 to 5 cm, slightly domed, paler as they dry; brown gills; thin brown stem darker toward the base with a small, fragile, brownish ring. One specimen lying on its side showing the gills and ring.",
"cepe": "Penny bun, cep (Boletus edulis). One whole mushroom: chestnut-brown, bun-shaped, smooth cap; underneath a spongy layer of tiny PORES (no gills), white to yellow-green; thick bulging pale stem covered at the top with a fine raised white NET pattern. Second specimen cut lengthwise showing firm white flesh that does NOT change colour.",
"girolle": "Chanterelle (Cantharellus cibarius). Two or three egg-yolk yellow mushrooms with an irregular, wavy, funnel-shaped cap; underneath thick, blunt, forked, vein-like RIDGES running down onto the stem (NOT sharp separate gills). One specimen torn lengthwise showing firm white flesh.",
"piedmouton": "Hedgehog mushroom (Hydnum repandum). An irregular cream to pale orange cap; the underside covered with small, crowded, fragile pale SPINES hanging down like teeth (NO gills, NO pores); short thick whitish stem. Second specimen turned over to show the spines clearly.",
"coulemelle": "Parasol mushroom (Macrolepiota procera). One tall mature mushroom 30 cm high: large flat cap 20 cm with a dark central bump and concentric brown scales on a pale background; free white gills; tall slender stem with brown snakeskin banding; a thick double ring that slides up and down; bulbous base. Second: a young closed specimen like a drumstick.",
"trompette": "Horn of plenty (Craterellus cornucopioides). A group of thin-fleshed, grey-black trumpet-shaped funnels, hollow down to the base, flared wavy rim; outside smooth or slightly wrinkled ash-grey, no gills. Among a few dead beech leaves. One specimen split lengthwise showing it is hollow.",
"pleurote": "Oyster mushroom (Pleurotus ostreatus). Overlapping, shelf-like, oyster-shell-shaped grey-blue to brown caps growing in layers from a piece of dead wood, with little or no stem; white gills running down to the point of attachment.",
"vesse": "Giant puffball (Calvatia gigantea). A large smooth white ball 30 cm across lying in grass, no visible stem. Second specimen cut in half showing pure white, uniform, firm flesh like mozzarella, with no outline of a cap or gills inside.",
"morille": "Morel (Morchella esculenta). One whole mushroom: pale yellow-brown cap covered in a honeycomb of deep irregular pits and ridges, cap joined directly to the white stem along its lower edge. Second specimen cut lengthwise showing it is ENTIRELY hollow as one single chamber from cap to stem base.",
"boletbai": "Bay bolete (Imleria badia). Chestnut-brown, slightly sticky cap; yellow PORES underneath; one spot pressed on the pores turned blue; slender brown stem without a net pattern. Second specimen cut lengthwise showing pale flesh with a slight blue tint above the pores.",
"panthere": "Panther cap (Amanita pantherina). Brown cap scattered with small pure white flakes; white gills; white stem with a smooth ring that does not have grooves; bulbous base with a neat rim (like the edge of a sock) at the top of the bulb. Second specimen lying on its side showing the gills and bulb.",
"vireuse": "Destroying angel (Amanita virosa). One entirely pure white mushroom: smooth, often cone-shaped or lopsided cap; white gills; shaggy, scaly white stem with a fragile ring; at the base a large white membranous sac-like volva. Second specimen cut lengthwise, all white.",
"cortinaire": "Fool's webcap (Cortinarius orellanus). Two medium mushrooms on mossy ground under oak: dry, matt, finely fibrous, tawny-orange to rusty-brown cap, slightly umbonate; thick, widely spaced, rusty-orange to cinnamon gills; slender yellowish-orange stem with fine fibres, the SAME width from top to base. NO membranous ring, NO skirt, NO collar on the stem: at most a few faint rust-coloured cobweb threads on the stem. NO volva, NO bulb.",
"entolome": "Livid pinkgill (Entoloma sinuatum). A large fleshy mushroom: grey-cream to pale grey-brown cap with a wavy, irregular edge; gills yellowish in a young specimen and salmon-PINK in the older one; stout white stem without ring or volva.",
"hypholome": "Sulphur tuft (Hypholoma fasciculare). A dense cluster on a rotting stump: small sulphur-yellow caps with an orange-brown centre; gills greenish-yellow in young ones and dark purple-brown in older ones; thin curved yellow stems.",
"rosedespres": "Field mushroom (Agaricus campestris). Silky white cap; free gills bright PINK in the young specimen and chocolate brown in the older one (never white); short white stem with a thin simple ring and NO volva, clean narrow base. In short pasture grass.",
"coprin": "Shaggy ink cap (Coprinus comatus). Three stages side by side: a young tall white cylindrical cap covered in shaggy woolly scales; an older one whose lower cap edge turns pink then black; an old one dissolving into black inky drips. Thin loose ring on the white stem.",
"piedbleu": "Wood blewit (Lepista nuda). A fleshy mushroom with a smooth lilac to violet-brown cap; crowded lilac gills; stout lilac-violet stem without ring or volva. Among fallen leaves.",
"mousseron": "St George's mushroom (Calocybe gambosa). Thick, fleshy, cream-white mushrooms with a smooth cap, very crowded white gills and a stout white stem, growing in a short arc in spring grass.",
"fauxmousseron": "Fairy ring champignon (Marasmius oreades). Small buff-beige mushrooms with a central bump, widely spaced cream gills and a thin tough stem; one stem twisted like a rope without breaking. Part of a fairy ring in short lawn grass.",
"armillaire": "Honey fungus (Armillaria mellea). A dense clump at the base of a tree trunk: honey-yellow caps with small dark hairy scales at the centre; white to cream gills; stems with a white cottony ring; black bootlace-like cords under loose bark.",
"collybie": "Velvet shank (Flammulina velutipes). A cluster on a dead branch with frost: small bright orange, slimy, shiny caps; pale yellow gills; stems smooth yellow at the top and dark brown-black VELVETY toward the base.",
"oreillejudas": "Jelly ear (Auricularia auricula-judae). Several brown, rubbery, translucent ear-shaped fruit bodies with a velvety outer surface and veined inner surface, growing on a dead elder branch.",
"polypore": "Chicken of the woods (Laetiporus sulphureus). Large overlapping fan-shaped brackets growing on an oak trunk: bright orange on top with a sulphur-yellow margin, sulphur-yellow pore surface underneath, no stems.",
"languedeboeuf": "Beefsteak fungus (Fistulina hepatica). A tongue-shaped, liver-red, moist bracket on an oak trunk. Second piece cut through showing streaky red marbled flesh like meat oozing red juice; underside cream with tiny separate tubes.",
"chanterelletube": "Winter chanterelle (Craterellus tubaeformis). A group of small mushrooms with thin brown funnel-shaped caps often with a hole in the centre, grey-yellow vein-like ridges underneath (no true gills) and hollow yellow stems, on moss.",
"russulecharbon": "Charcoal burner (Russula cyanoxantha). A mushroom with a cap mixing violet, lilac and green tones; crowded white gills that bend without breaking; white stem. Second specimen broken showing white chalk-like crumbly flesh.",
"rougissante": "Blusher (Amanita rubescens). Pinkish-brown cap with grey-beige flakes; white gills; white stem with a ring striated on its upper surface; bulbous base; flesh turning pinkish-red where damaged, show a slug-nibbled spot and a cut base reddening.",
"printaniere": "Fool's mushroom (Amanita verna). One entirely white mushroom: smooth white cap, white gills, white stem with a ring, large white sac-like volva at the base. Spring setting with a few young leaves. Second specimen cut lengthwise, all white.",
"lepiote": "Deadly dapperling (Lepiota brunneoincarnata). A small mushroom 3 to 5 cm: cap with concentric pinkish-brown scales darker at the centre; free white gills; short stem with pinkish-brown belt-like zones on its lower half, no distinct ring. Shown on grass with a small acorn for scale.",
"gyromitre": "False morel (Gyromitra esculenta). A red-brown, wrinkled, brain-like cap with rounded lobes on a short pale stem. Second specimen cut lengthwise showing the inside divided into several irregular chambers, NOT one single hollow.",
"omphalote": "Jack-o'-lantern (Omphalotus olearius). A dense tuft of bright orange funnel-shaped mushrooms growing from the base of an olive tree stump, with true, crowded, sharp-edged orange gills running down the curved stems.",
"paxille": "Brown roll-rim (Paxillus involutus). A brown mushroom whose cap edge is ROLLED inward; yellowish-tan gills running down the stem, with a spot bruised dark brown; short brown stem. Under birch with a birch leaf beside.",
"equestre": "Man on horseback (Tricholoma equestre). A fleshy mushroom with a greenish-yellow cap browner at the centre, sulphur-yellow gills and a yellow stem, in sandy soil under pine needles.",
"tigre": "Tiger tricholoma (Tricholoma pardinum). A large fleshy mushroom with a pale grey cap covered in darker grey-brown scales in concentric rings, giving a tiger-like pattern; cream gills; stout white stem.",
"clitoblanc": "Fool's funnel (Clitocybe rivulosa). Small whitish mushrooms with a flat to slightly depressed cap looking frosted or powdered, crowded gills running down the stem, in a lawn.",
"noirdencre": "Common ink cap (Coprinopsis atramentaria). A cluster of grey, bell-shaped, pleated caps on short white stems; older caps dissolving at the edge into black ink drips.",
"emetique": "The sickener (Russula emetica). A mushroom with a bright cherry-red smooth shiny cap; pure white gills; pure white stem. Second specimen broken showing crumbly white flesh. Among moss and pine needles.",
"satan": "Devil's bolete (Rubroboletus satanas). A large bolete with a pale whitish-grey cap; blood-red pores; bulging stem covered with a red net pattern; second specimen cut showing pale flesh turning blue.",
"psilocybe": "Liberty cap (Psilocybe semilanceata). Small slender mushrooms with a pointed conical beige-brown cap with a sharp nipple and a long thin wavy stem, in damp pasture grass.",
"lactaire": "Saffron milk cap (Lactarius deliciosus). An orange cap with darker concentric rings, slightly depressed in the centre; orange gills; one cut gill oozing bright CARROT-ORANGE milk; some spots on the cap turned green. Among pine needles.",
# ---------------- ANIMAUX ----------------
"sanglier": "Wild boar (Sus scrofa): an adult boar in side view, dark grey-brown bristly coat, long snout, small tusks. Corner vignette: its footprint in mud, two pointed hoof toes with the two dew claws clearly marked behind.",
"cerf": "Red deer (Cervus elaphus): a stag in side view, reddish-brown coat, pale rump patch, large branched antlers. Corner vignette: its elongated heart-shaped cloven hoof print, 6 to 9 cm.",
"renard": "Red fox (Vulpes vulpes): a fox in side view, orange-red coat, white chin and chest, black legs, bushy tail with a white tip. Corner vignette: its narrow oval paw print with 4 toes and visible claws.",
"tique": "Castor bean tick (Ixodes ricinus): one adult female tick greatly enlarged, seen from above: 8 legs, dark brown-black front shield and mouthparts, red-brown body behind. Small vignette: an engorged grey tick and a nymph on a fingertip for scale.",
"castor": "Eurasian beaver (Castor fiber): a beaver in side view sitting on a riverbank, brown fur, flat scaly paddle-shaped tail. Corner vignette: a tree trunk gnawed into a pencil point with wood chips around it.",
"vipere": "Common European adder (Vipera berus): a stocky short snake coiled on dry leaves, grey-brown with a continuous dark ZIGZAG stripe along the back; head enlarged in a vignette showing the vertical slit pupil and a dark V or X mark on the head.",
"loup": "Grey wolf (Canis lupus): a wolf in side view, larger and leaner than a dog, grey-beige coat with darker back, long legs. Corner vignette: its oval paw print with 4 toes and claws, about 10 cm.",
"chevreuil": "Roe deer (Capreolus capreolus): a roe deer in side view, reddish-brown coat, white rump patch, small upright 3-pointed antlers on the buck. Corner vignette: small heart-shaped cloven hoof print 4 to 5 cm.",
"blaireau": "European badger (Meles meles): a badger in side view, grey body, black and white striped head. Corner vignette: its broad paw print with 5 toes in a row and long claw marks.",
"salamandre": "Fire salamander (Salamandra salamandra): a black salamander with bold irregular yellow blotches walking on wet moss.",
"processionnaire": "Oak processionary caterpillars (Thaumetopoea processionea): a group of grey hairy caterpillars clustered on oak bark next to a whitish silk nest. Small vignette: one caterpillar enlarged.",
"frelon": "European hornet and common wasp side by side: hornet larger (3 cm), reddish-brown and yellow; wasp smaller, black and yellow, with a narrow waist. Both seen from above, wings spread.",
"aspic": "Asp viper (Vipera aspis): a stocky snake coiled on stones, grey-brown with dark crossbars or a broken zigzag along the back; vignette of the head with slightly upturned snout and vertical slit pupil.",
"processionpin": "Pine processionary caterpillars (Thaumetopoea pityocampa): a single-file line of brown-orange hairy caterpillars walking nose-to-tail on the ground. Vignette: a white silk nest at the tip of a pine branch.",
"chamois": "Chamois (Rupicapra rupicapra): a chamois on a rock in side view, brown coat, white face with dark stripes through the eyes, short black horns hooked backward at the tips.",
"marmotte": "Alpine marmot (Marmota marmota): a plump grey-brown marmot sitting upright next to its burrow entrance among stones and alpine grass.",
"patou": "Livestock guardian dog (Great Pyrenees type): a large white dog standing calmly beside a few sheep in a mountain pasture.",
"vive": "Lesser weever fish (Echiichthys vipera): a small fish 12 cm, yellow-brown, half buried in sand with only the eyes and the small black spiny first dorsal fin showing; second view of the whole fish in side view.",
"meduse": "Two jellyfish side by side as a naturalist plate: a lion's mane jellyfish with a reddish bell and long hair-like tentacles, and a compass jellyfish with a pale bell marked with brown V-shaped lines and long tentacles.",
# ---------------- POISSONS ----------------
"truite": "Brown trout (Salmo trutta) in full side view: streamlined body, olive-brown back, golden flanks with black spots and red spots ringed with pale halos, a small fleshy adipose fin without rays between the dorsal fin and the square tail.",
"perche": "European perch (Perca fluviatilis) in full side view: greenish body with 5 to 7 dark vertical bars, a spiny first dorsal fin with a black spot at its rear, bright orange-red pelvic and anal fins.",
"brochet": "Northern pike (Esox lucius) in full side view: long torpedo-shaped body, duck-bill-shaped flat snout, green flanks with pale bean-shaped spots, dorsal and anal fins set far back near the tail. Small vignette: open mouth with many sharp teeth.",
"sandre": "Zander (Sander lucioperca) in full side view: long grey-green body with blurred dark bands, two separate dorsal fins, the first spiny, large glassy eye, a few large fang-like teeth visible.",
"gardon": "Roach (Rutilus rutilus) in full side view: small silvery fish with blue-green back, RED iris, reddish pelvic and anal fins.",
"chevesne": "Chub (Squalius cephalus) in full side view: thick body, large broad head, big scales edged in black forming a net pattern, convex orange-red anal fin.",
"carpe": "Common carp (Cyprinus carpio) in full side view: deep golden-bronze body with large scales, long dorsal fin, FOUR barbels around the mouth (two short, two longer).",
"barbeau": "Barbel (Barbus barbus) in full side view: long body with flat belly, underslung mouth with four fleshy barbels, brown-green back, reddish fins.",
"silure": "Wels catfish (Silurus glanis) in full side view: very long scaleless slimy dark body, broad flat head, wide mouth with two very long barbels and four short ones under the chin, tiny dorsal fin, very long anal fin reaching the tail.",
"poissonchat": "Black bullhead (Ameiurus melas) in full side view: scaleless dark brown body, broad head, eight barbels around the mouth, one hard spine at the front of the dorsal fin and of each pectoral fin, small adipose fin.",
"anguille": "European eel (Anguilla anguilla) in full side view: snake-like body, small head, small eyes, no pelvic fins, dorsal, tail and anal fins merged into one continuous fringe around the rear of the body, dark back and yellowish belly.",
"saumon": "Atlantic salmon (Salmo salar): adult in full side view, silvery body with small black X-shaped spots above the lateral line, forked tail, small adipose fin. Smaller vignette below: a young parr with a row of dark finger-mark blotches along the side.",
"ombre": "Grayling (Thymallus thymallus) in full side view: grey-silver body with a few black spots on the front, a very large sail-like purple-red dorsal fin with dark spots, small adipose fin.",
"chabot": "European bullhead (Cottus gobio) in full side view and from above: small fish under 15 cm with a very large flat head, large fan-shaped pectoral fins, brown marbled scaleless body, lying on river pebbles.",
"ecrevisse_rouge": "Noble crayfish (Astacus astacus) seen from above: dark brown crayfish, large broad granular claws; one claw turned over showing a bright red underside.",
"ecrevisse_signal": "Signal crayfish (Pacifastacus leniusculus) seen from above: blue-brown crayfish with smooth claws, a white or turquoise patch at the hinge of each claw, red claw underside.",
"grandevive": "Greater weever (Trachinus draco) in full side view: long yellow-brown body up to 40 cm with thin dark oblique stripes, a short black spiny first dorsal fin, eyes high on the head.",
"rascasse": "Black scorpionfish (Scorpaena porcus) in full side view: stocky red-brown marbled body covered with small skin flaps, large spiny head, big eyes, spiny dorsal fin raised.",
"vairon": "Eurasian minnow (Phoxinus phoxinus): a small group of tiny minnows under 10 cm in side view, flanks marbled with dark blotches, one male with a red belly.",
}
